# Line endings are LF everywhere, including on a Windows checkout.
#
# Not a style preference. Two things in this repository hash file contents and
# compare the result: `lib/evidence.js` digests a receipt so an edited one can be
# refused, and `lib/slice.js` digests a diff so a stale verification cannot pass
# as a fresh one. CRLF changes the bytes, so the same file checked out on Windows
# produces a different digest and both checks fail against evidence nobody
# touched — which is the one failure they exist to report.
#
# The SPDX header check reads the same way: it compares the first bytes of every
# module against a constant written with \n.
#
# `bin/pdkit` needs it for a third reason. A shebang line followed by \r makes
# the kernel look for an interpreter named "node\r", and the plugin puts that
# file on PATH.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so git leaves them alone.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.pdf binary
